76:## OAuth as a Pre-step
78:OAuth2 is supported by this API through a cert-only **`client_credentials`** grant. The TPP obtains a
79:single access token by calling `POST /oauth2/token` over an mTLS connection presenting its eIDAS QWAC
80:certificate — there is **no** browser-based PSU login, **no** authorization code, and **no** token
96:    TPP->>N26: POST /oauth2/token<br/>grant_type=client_credentials (eIDAS QWAC cert)
99:    TPP->>N26: POST /consents<br/>Authorization: Bearer access_token
109:| **How to get** | Call `POST /oauth2/token` with `grant_type=client_credentials` over mTLS with your eIDAS QWAC certificate. No PSU login or authorization code is required. | Existing refresh token |
129:## Authentication endpoints
131:These endpoints are used to retrieve an access or refresh token for use with the /consents and /accounts endpoints.
137:The TPP obtains a cert-only `client_credentials` access token bound to its eIDAS QWAC certificate. This single token is used to create the consent and call the AIS endpoints after SCA — no PSU login and no authorization code exchange take place.
