125:## Redirect (App-to-App) SCA approach
127:Alongside the `DECOUPLED` flow described above, the sandbox also supports the **Redirect (App-to-App)** SCA approach. This lets you test the redirect flow end-to-end without a real N26 app: dedicated sandbox endpoints stand in for the PSU approving (or declining) in the app.
129:### Requesting the redirect approach
135:| `TPP-Redirect-Preferred` | `true`                         | Opts into the Redirect (App-to-App) approach.                     |
136:| `TPP-Redirect-URI`       | `https://tpp.example.com/cb`   | Mandatory when redirect is preferred. Must be a valid URL.        |
139:> :information_source: In the sandbox the redirect approach is honoured whenever `TPP-Redirect-Preferred: true` is sent. If `TPP-Redirect-URI` is missing or malformed, the request is rejected with `400 Bad Request`.
141:The create response returns the `ASPSP-SCA-Approach: REDIRECT` header and an `scaRedirect` link that, in production, points the PSU to the N26 app:
145:ASPSP-SCA-Approach: REDIRECT
151:        "scaRedirect": {
152:            "href": "https://app.n26.com/wl/open-banking/aisp?consentId=fb44eb9c-d12f-4aef-90bd-726c47f2e864"
161:> :information_source: For AISP, the redirect approach only supports the **bank-offered** consent shape (empty `accounts`, `balances` and `transactions` arrays); the PSU selects the accounts during the SCA. Any other access shape is rejected with `400 Bad Request`.
163:### OAuth pre-step (redirect)
165:For the redirect approach, obtain the access token with the cert-only `client_credentials` grant. You do **not** need the `/oauth2/authorize` or `generate-auth-code` steps described above.
167:The `role` query parameter carries the scope and must be one of `DEDICATED_AISP`, `DEDICATED_PISP` or `DEDICATED_CBPII`. The `client_id` (your TPP id) is derived from the eIDAS QWAC certificate presented over the mTLS connection.
176:client_id={{tpp-id}}&
187:| client_id    | Your TPP id (`{{tpp-id}}`), derived from the eIDAS QWAC certificate.                             |
191:### Simulating the Redirect SCA
197:| AISP  | `POST /sandbox/psu-interaction/redirect/consents/{consentId}/scas`             |
198:| CBPII | `POST /sandbox/psu-interaction/redirect/confirmation-of-funds-consents/{consentId}/scas` |
199:| PISP  | `POST /sandbox/psu-interaction/redirect/payments/{paymentId}/scas`             |
204:POST /sandbox/psu-interaction/redirect/consents/{consentId}/scas HTTP/1.1
215:    "redirectUri": "https://tpp.example.com/cb?state=xyz",
221:On `REJECTED`, the `consentStatus` becomes `rejected`, the `scaStatus` becomes `failed`, and the `redirectUri` carries an error, e.g. `https://tpp.example.com/cb?error=access_denied&state=xyz`.
228:    "redirectUri": "https://tpp.example.com/cb?state=xyz"
232:The `redirectUri` is the callback URL the N26 app would redirect the PSU to once the SCA completes. After simulating the SCA, poll the consent or payment status as usual.
