## 2026-09-26 STEP 1 — DELTA

Provenance of this cycle's delta: the vendor's own public API corpus (`github.com/n26/psd2-tpp-docs`, already in `reports/reposcan-findings.md`) was used to extract the **real** route table instead of a generic wordlist. 46 read-only GETs, ≤1.2 s spacing, no POST/HEAD/OPTIONS, no state created.

[NEW] @ xs2a.tech26.de: **production Berlin-Group XS2A API (AIS+PIS) is LIVE and Bearer-gated** at the documented base `https://xs2a.tech26.de/v1/berlin-group/v1` — 11 route classes → `401 len=0` with `x-envoy-upstream-service-time` (app-layer, not edge): `/accounts`, `/accounts/{id}`, `/accounts/{id}/balances`, `/accounts/{id}/transactions`, `/accounts/{id}/transactions/{tid}`, `/consents`, `/consents/status`, `/consents/{id}`, `/consents/{id}/status`, `/payments/sepa-credit-transfers/{id}`, `/payments/sepa-credit-transfers/{id}/status`. Absent (404): top-level `/balances`, `/transactions`, `/funds-confirmations/{id}`, `/berlin-group/v1/*` (missing `/v1`). **Invalidates the KB closure "aisp/xs2a carry no legacy family / route-less"** — that was a path-family false negative.
[NEW] @ xs2a.tech26.de: **gate is not a blind prefix-firewall** — bogus route `/v1/berlin-group/v1/this-route-does-not-exist-xyz` → `404` while real routes → `401`. Route existence is therefore **anonymously distinguishable** here, unlike api.tech26.de (uniform 401).
[NEW] @ xs2a.tech26.de: **mTLS is not enforced at the production edge.** ELB is named `obnium-mtls-live-fra` (Berlin Group mandates eIDAS QWAC mTLS on every TPP request), yet an anonymous client completes a TLSv1.3 handshake **with no client certificate** and reaches the app (`401`). The only gate is a bearer token.
[NEW] @ xs2a-staging / aisp-staging / pisp-staging.tech26.de (never probed; surfaced by certspotter, 39 names): all CNAME to **`obnium-mtls-staging-fra-558276106`** ELB (pre-production twin of the live XS2A tier) but are **SG-gated — connect-timeout 15 s, 0 B** on 443. Zero anonymous reachability; mTLS posture of the staging twin unassessable.
[NEW] @ xs2a.tech26.de: token-minting surface is **not anonymously reachable** — `/oauth2/token`, `/v1/berlin-group/v1/oauth2/token`, `/oauth2/authorize` all `404`; documented sandbox helpers (`/sandbox/oauth2/authorize`, `/sandbox/oauth2/token`, `/sandbox/psu-interaction/generate-auth-code/{id}`) are **404 on the production host** → sandbox/prod path separation holds (closes the unauthenticated-auth-code-minting risk; no false report).
[CHANGED] @ aisp.tech26.de + pisp.tech26.de: sharing the `{aisp,xs2a,pisp}` cert leaf (Amazon RSA 2048 M04, valid 2026-02-02→2027-03-03), they **do not** serve the Berlin-Group table (`404` app-layer, est=1ms) — the "mesh split" recorded 09-25 is really *host-specific routing*: xs2a alone terminates BG routes. aisp/pisp remain **unmapped for their own** route table (not "route-less").
[CHANGED] @ app.n26.com: vendor-documented open-banking routes exist — `/wl/open-banking/aisp?consentId=` → `302 /open-banking/aisp?consentId=…` → unauth `302 /login?…&redirect=%2Fopen-banking%3F…`.
[NEW] REJECTED-class closed: open-redirect attempt on that `redirect` param — the server **reconstructs** `redirect` from the matched route path and ignores the user-supplied value (`?redirect=https://example.com/`, `//example.com/`, `/%5Cexample.com/` → all `redirect=%2Fopen-banking`); path-smuggling variants (`//example.com/open-banking`, `/%2F%2F…`, `/.//…`, `/\…` with `--path-as-is`) → `404`. No open redirect.
[CHANGED] @ process: first non-NO_DELTA cycle since 2026-09-17 (~9 days). Break came from **corpus-driven route mapping** (vendor OpenAPI + Postman + CT), not from re-probing frozen boundaries — and the frozen-boundary re-probing canon stayed correct.

