## STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES
[HYP] Missing mTLS / strong-authentication enforcement on the public Berlin-Group XS2A production API
class: MISCONFIG
asset: xs2a.tech26.de/v1/berlin-group/v1
confidence: 70
reasoning: 11 route classes of the live AIS+PIS API return 401 at the app layer behind ELB `obnium-mtls-live-fra`; an anonymous client completes TLSv1.3 with no client certificate and still reaches the app, so the client-certificate requirement the ELB name and the Berlin Group interface specification impose is not enforced at the transport edge; the sole gate is a bearer token; the documented pre-production twin `xs2a-staging.tech26.de` sits on `obnium-mtls-staging-fra` and is SG-gated, so the live tier is the only anonymously reachable one
evidence_needed: a QWAC client certificate plus a token issued for a registered TPP, proving the app never binds the certificate CN to the token's client_id, or proving a token minted without any QWAC is accepted on these routes
verify_steps: `GET /v1/berlin-group/v1/consents/<tpp-A-consent-id> HTTP/2` + `Host: xs2a.tech26.de` + `Authorization: Bearer <tpp-A-token>` with no client certificate (baseline) and with a QWAC cert whose CN differs from the token's client_id; compare status and any WWW-Authenticate/ASPSP-SCA-* headers
impact: mandatory PSD2 strong customer authentication is reduced to bearer-token possession, so any leaked, stale or mis-issued token yields full account listing, balances, transaction history, consent state and SEPA payment initiation for the linked PSU; HIGH, conditional on token compromise, no anonymous access established
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] api.tech26.de BOLA on the legacy account-resource family
class: IDOR
asset: api.tech26.de/api/accounts/{id}/{tans|statements|addresses|bookings|cards|approvals|transactions|transfer|beneficiaries|devices|limits|cosmetics}
confidence: 92
reasoning: 15 unversioned members return byte-identical `401 len=211` `invalid_token` problem+json (`md5 d58528c924`); account IDs 1,2,3,4,9 gate identically; GET-only route table; path-shape, case, query-param and header-shape variants all closed; gate confirmed shared with beta-api.tech26.de and sapi.tech26.de
evidence_needed: two isolated sandbox identities, read-only Bearer tokens, stable synthetic account/resource IDs, and object-bearing responses for both
verify_steps: `GET /api/me HTTP/1.1` + `Host: api.tech26.de` + `Authorization: Bearer <sandbox-A-read-only>`; then `GET /api/accounts/<sandbox-B-account-id>/statements` with token A and the mirror with token B; halt on any non-test data
impact: conditional cross-tenant disclosure of statements, address PII, cards, TANs, devices, limits; CRITICAL if object-level authorization is missing
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] pay.n26.com Stripe-forwarded payment API BOLA
class: IDOR
asset: pay.n26.com/v1/{payments,balance,charges,customers,invoices}
confidence: 85
reasoning: 23+ versioned routes return Stripe-shaped 401 with distinct no-key (`len=342`) and invalid-key (`len=132`) bodies, `WWW-Authenticate: Basic realm="Stripe"`, `ACAO: *`; OAuth/Connect routes 404 identically to direct Stripe, proving 1:1 passthrough with no N26 authorization layer; key discovery closed on 3/3 corpora
evidence_needed: a coordinator-approved test-mode key accepted by this host, synthetic payment/customer/charge fixtures, and proof that object ownership is enforced independently of the key
verify_steps: `GET /v1/payments?limit=3 HTTP/1.1` + `Host: pay.n26.com` + `Authorization: Bearer <approved-test-key>`; then `/v1/balance`, `/v1/charges/<fixture-id>`, `/v1/customers/<fixture-id>` with the same and a second approved key; do not enumerate live IDs
impact: conditional cross-account payment, charge, customer and balance disclosure; CRITICAL, no anonymous exposure established
testability: AUTH_HELPED

## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE
[PARKED] cross-deployment token audience confusion ({api,beta-api,sapi} + live/staging XS2A pair) — upgraded with `xs2a-staging.tech26.de` on `obnium-mtls-staging-fra` but still speculative at 55; it is the natural follow-on to hypothesis 1 and should be run in the same credentialed session rather than as a separate claim. Also parked: keyless signed-WebSocket-token replay (70).
[FINAL] 1. xs2a.tech26.de missing mTLS/SCA enforcement on the live Berlin-Group API (70, only hypothesis this cycle backed by a new observation); 2. api.tech26.de BOLA (92); 3. pay.n26.com Stripe-forwarded BOLA (85). No anonymous result is promoted as a finding.

## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION
[NEXT] HUMAN: Provision one TPP test credential for the Berlin-Group tier — a QWAC client certificate plus its `client_id`, or a bearer minted for `xs2a.tech26.de` — so two things can be settled in one session: (a) `GET /v1/berlin-group/v1/consents/<id> HTTP/2` + `Host: xs2a.tech26.de` + `Authorization: Bearer <tpp-token>` with **no** client certificate vs with a QWAC whose CN ≠ the token's client_id (does the app bind cert to token?); (b) the BOLA matrix — TPP-A's token against TPP-B's `consentId`, `accountId` and `transactions/{id}`. Do **not** attempt `POST /oauth2/token` or `POST /consents` on the live tier without explicit written approval.

## STEP 6 — LEARNING
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: the live Berlin-Group XS2A API (AIS+PIS) is at `/v1/berlin-group/v1` with 11 Bearer-gated route classes, and mTLS is not enforced at the edge despite the `obnium-mtls-live-fra` ELB — anonymous TLS1.3 completes with no client certificate.
[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ app.n26.com `/open-banking`: open-redirect hypothesis closed — the `redirect` param is rebuilt server-side from the matched route path, user-supplied absolute/protocol-relative values are ignored, and path-smuggling variants 404.
[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: unauthenticated auth-code minting via the documented sandbox helpers (`/sandbox/oauth2/authorize|/sandbox/oauth2/token|/sandbox/psu-interaction/generate-auth-code/{id}`) is **not** present on the production host — sandbox and production are path-separated.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ {aisp,pisp}.tech26.de: not "route-less" and not a mesh split — they share the `{aisp,xs2a,pisp}` cert leaf but do not terminate the Berlin-Group table; their own route tables are still unenumerated.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ process: after ~9 days of NO_DELTA, the only thing that produced signal was **vendor-corpus-driven route mapping** (public OpenAPI yml + Postman collection + certspotter), not further anonymous boundary probing. Generalised rule: when a gate returns `401` for real routes and `404` for absent ones, the vendor's own API corpus is the correct enumeration source; when every path returns `401`, only a known-real route table can produce trustworthy negatives.

## STEP 7 — RISK
[RISK] N26 Bank AG: 92 — a whole previously-unmapped production API class (Berlin-Group AIS+PIS on xs2a.tech26.de: accounts, balances, transactions, consents, SEPA payment initiation) was assumed absent for 9 days, and its only transport-layer control (the mTLS posture the ELB name advertises) is not enforced for internet clients. Combined with the two standing credential-gated IDOR paths and the unreachable staging twin, undetected exposure in the open-banking tier is the dominant residual risk. Still zero validated findings and zero anonymous data access; every path remains bearer-gated.
