## STEP 1 — DELTA

[NEW] @ aisp.tech26.de: **route table mapped from vendor corpus (psd2-tpp-docs/doc/fallback-aisp.md)** — this is the **PSD2 Fallback / contingency** interface, not Berlin Group. 4 live route classes, all `401` app-layer: `GET /api/v2/accounts`, `GET /api/v2/accounts/{accountId}`, `GET /api/fallback/accounts/{accountId}/transactions?from&to`, `GET /api/fallback/accounts/{accountId}/transactions/{transactionId}`. **Invalidates** the 09-26 KB entry "aisp/pisp own route tables still unenumerated" — they were never 404, they were probed with the wrong wordlist (`/api/me`, `/api/accounts/1/statements` = the api-family shapes).

[NEW] @ pisp.tech26.de: **route table mapped (fallback-pisp.md)** — 5 live route classes: `GET /api/openbanking/fallback/sepa-ct/{paymentId}/status`, `.../sepa-instant/{paymentId}/status`, `.../so/{paymentId}/status` (all `401`), plus documented POST payment-initiation `/api/openbanking/fallback/sepa-ct`, `.../sepa-instant`, `/api/transactions/so`. **Live payment-initiation surface on the contingency interface** — highest-value money-movement asset in the program, previously absent from the inventory.

[NEW] @ {xs2a,aisp,pisp}.tech26.de: all three CNAME to the **same** ELB `obnium-mtls-live-fra-328671153.eu-central-1.elb.amazonaws.com` (63.184.77.225 / 18.195.172.188 / 35.156.254.129). Routing is vhost-based at one Istio gateway — not a "mesh split".

[NEW] @ {xs2a,aisp,pisp}.tech26.de: **mTLS definitively absent** — `openssl s_client -tls1_3` with no client cert returns `No client certificate CA names sent` on all three, i.e. the server never issues a TLS `CertificateRequest`. N26's own public support page states of aisp/pisp: *"Access to the above URL and establishing the TLS connection requires implementation of a qualified certificate."* Documented control is not enforced at the transport layer.

[NEW] @ app.n26.com: `/wl/open-banking/cbpii?consentId=x` → `302 /open-banking/cbpii?consentId=x` → unauth `302 /login?...&redirect=%2Fopen-banking%2Fcbpii%3F...`. **Third open-banking web surface** (cbpii = funds-confirmation), previously only `aisp` was known. `/wl/open-banking/pisp?consentId=x` → `302 /feed` (route absent, silently absorbed into the authenticated feed).

[CHANGED] @ xs2a.tech26.de: the 09-26 REJECTED conclusion *"token-minting surface is not anonymously reachable — `/oauth2/token` 404"* is **unsound**. On this edge, `GET /api/mfa/challenge` (documented POST-only, confirmed live) returns a **byte-identical 404** to `GET /oauth2/token`. GET-404 does not discriminate absent from POST-only here — the same method-gating asymmetry already proven on `api.tech26.de` (`GET /api/me`→401, `HEAD /api/me`→404). The password/refresh grant surface is **unresolved, not closed**.

