[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ app.n26.com `/open-banking/{aisp,cbpii}`: `state` is passed through as an opaque query param into the server-rebuilt `/login?...&redirect=` chain, and `redirect` is server-constructed from the matched route path (09-26 finding holds) — no open redirect and no observable state-binding failure; auth-code theft on the new Redirect SCA mode is AUTH_HELPED at best, not reportable.
[LEARN] REJECTED AUTH @ pisp.tech26.de + aisp.tech26.de: the "the TPP must not use access/refresh tokens on other base URLs" and "PISP tokens cannot be used for AISP flows" audience-separation controls **are enforced at the routing layer** — the three route tables are strictly disjoint per Host, so a token minted on one host has no route to reach on another. Closes the cross-deployment audience-confusion item parked at 55 last cycle.
[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de `/oauth2/token`: my own 09-26 entry "token-minting surface is not anonymously reachable" is retracted as unsound — `GET /api/mfa/challenge` (documented POST-only, confirmed live) returns a byte-identical 404 on this edge, so GET-404 cannot distinguish absent from POST-only. Generalised rule: on this program, a 404 on a GET is only evidence of route absence for routes documented as GET; for documented-POST routes it is evidence of nothing.

