reasoning: the sandbox data plane and the live data plane are **co-tenants on one production host** behind one Istio gateway, 7 vs 21 route classes, both `401` app-layer, both vhost-identical (`server: istio-envoy`, no distinguishing header). The authorization plane for both tiers is **anonymously reachable** (`401` at `/oauth2/authorize` and `/sandbox/oauth2/authorize` with documented parameters, `404` without — parameter presence, not method, is the discriminator). N26's own Postman collection shows the sandbox flow needs **no PSU interaction**: step `0.2 (Fake) Generate auth code` is `POST /sandbox/psu-interaction/generate-auth-code/{request_id}?role=DEDICATED_AISP` — the ASPSP issues the auth code itself. Registered `client_id`s are public (`PSDDE-BAFIN-000001`, `PSDES-BDE-3DFD12`). Two registered client_ids mean a token minted under `DEDICATED_AISP` is bound to a client, but the Berlin-Group spec requires ASPSP to reject sandbox tokens on the production service; the single-host, single-gateway topology makes an audience check easy to omit and there is no `aud`/`iss` claim in any observable response. Separately, `x-n26-userid` is a client-asserted PSU identity header in the same collection.
evidence_needed: a token minted against the **sandbox** issuer and replayed against the **live** data plane (`/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts`, `.../accounts/{id}/balances`, `.../payments/instant-sepa-credit-transfers`), and the reverse; plus the live/sandbox `aud`/`iss` values from the two token responses; plus a repeat of `/sandbox/.../accounts` with the `x-n26-userid` header swapped to a second fixture value.
verify_steps: baseline `GET /v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts HTTP/2` + `Host: xs2a.tech26.de` + `Authorization: Bearer <sandbox-token>` → expect `401`; then `GET /sandbox/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts` with the same sandbox token → expect `200`; then `GET /sandbox/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts` with `x-n26-userid: <second fixture uuid>` and compare bodies. Obtain the sandbox token with `GET /sandbox/oauth2/authorize?client_id=PSDDE-BAFIN-000001&scope=DEDICATED_AISP&code_challenge=w6uP8Tcg6K2QR905Rms8iXTlksL6OD1KOWBxTK7wxPI&redirect_uri=https://app.n26.com/login&response_type=CODE&state=<random>` then `POST /sandbox/psu-interaction/generate-auth-code/<request_id>?role=DEDICATED_AISP` then `POST /sandbox/oauth2/token?role=DEDICATED_AISP`. Halt on any non-sandbox data; do not touch live account IDs.
impact: a token obtainable with **zero user interaction and zero user credentials** that is accepted on the live tier yields account listing, balances, transaction history, consent state and **initiation of instant SEPA credit transfers** (irrevocable) as the linked PSU; combined with the absent mTLS, PSD2 SCA collapses to "possession of a sandbox-minted token". CRITICAL if confirmed; nothing anonymous is established today.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] Cross-tenant BOLA on the fallback PIS/AIS interface with client-asserted anti-fraud binding
class: IDOR
asset: pisp.tech26.de/api/openbanking/fallback/{sepa-ct,sepa-instant,so}/{paymentId}/status; aisp.tech26.de/api/fallback/accounts/{accountId}/transactions
confidence: 68
reasoning: reconfirmed live this cycle — `GET /api/openbanking/fallback/sepa-ct/1111.../status` → `401`, `GET /api/fallback/accounts/1111.../transactions?from=0&to=1` → `401`. Route table is the correct one (vendor `fallback-pisp.md` / `fallback-aisp.md`, not the api-family wordlist). `{accountId}`/`{paymentId}` are attacker-suppliable UUIDs. N26 documents the entire anti-fraud layer as keyed to a client-asserted header: *"providing this IP address guarantees us to identify proper user calls and to protect the integrity of our services… If a TPP doesn't provide an end-user's IP address… such cases will be treated in accordance to our established security policies."* `device-token` is a client-invented UUID v4 and `x-tpp-userip` is client-asserted on the same request.
evidence_needed: two isolated sandbox TPP sessions with stable synthetic `accountId`/`paymentId` per session, and object-bearing responses.
verify_steps: `GET /api/openbanking/fallback/sepa-ct/<tpp-B-payment-id>/status HTTP/1.1` + `Host: pisp.tech26.de` + `Authorization: bearer <tpp-A-access>` + `device-token: <uuid-A>` + `x-tpp-userip: <tpp-B-user's real IP>`; mirror with token B; same pattern on `GET /api/fallback/accounts/<tpp-B-accountId>/transactions?from=0&to=1` at `aisp.tech26.de`. Halt on any non-test data.
impact: cross-tenant disclosure of payment execution state, rejection reasons and full transaction history with counterparty identifiers; spoofing `x-tpp-userip` with the victim's real IP additionally neutralises the documented fraud controls, so a stolen fallback token is used without tripping IP-anomaly detection. CRITICAL conditional on BOLA; no anonymous access established.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] Unattended 180-day access to full account data via unbound fallback refresh-token chain
class: AUTH
asset: aisp.tech26.de/oauth2/token
confidence: 70
reasoning: the fallback AISP spec makes the access token 15-minute / `Storage: NEVER`, but the refresh token is a **180-day rotating chain** renewed by `POST /oauth2/token` with `grant_type=refresh_token`, requiring only `refresh_token` in the body plus the `device-token` **request header** — a value the doc tells the TPP to invent ("a valid UUID v4 as per RFC 4122"). `x-tpp-userip` is likewise client-asserted. The `/oauth2/token` route is POST-only, so the 09-26 `GET` 404 is uninformative — and this cycle proves the same edge answers `401` for `/oauth2/authorize` when parameters are present, so a `404` on a param-less GET carries no information at all.
evidence_needed: one fallback-tier sandbox refresh token plus a second independently-minted session, to test whether a refresh token issued to session A is accepted when replayed with a freshly invented `device-token` and a different `x-tpp-userip`.
verify_steps: baseline `GET /api/v2/accounts HTTP/1.1` + `Host: aisp.tech26.de` + `Authorization: bearer <tpp-A-access>` + `device-token: <uuid-A>` + `x-tpp-userip: 203.0.113.7`; repeat with `device-token: <random-uuid-B>` + `x-tpp-userip: 198.51.100.9` (both different from the minting session); compare status and body. Halt on any non-test data.
impact: if `device-token` is not bound server-side to the session, one leaked refresh token yields 180 days of unattended access to every account's IBAN, balance, product, owner name and full transaction history including counterparty IBANs; HIGH.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

[PARKED] xs2a.tech26.de missing mTLS/SCA enforcement: still true and still 78, but it is a transport-control gap (INFO/low as a bounty item) that is fully explained by the single-`obnium-mtls-live-fra`-gateway topology, and it is tested in the **same credentialed session** as hypothesis 1 — reporting it separately would duplicate the evidence.
[PARKED] sandbox plane serving production customer data: cannot be separated from hypothesis 1 without a sandbox token; folded into its verify steps rather than carried as a free-floating claim.
[PARKED] `POST /oauth2/token` reachability on xs2a.tech26.de: GET returns `404` on both tiers, which per my own 09-26 rule is evidence of nothing for a documented-POST route. Unresolved, not closed; not promoted.
[PARKED] vhost route confusion / token-audience bypass across `{xs2a,aisp,pisp}`: **refuted last cycle** — route tables strictly disjoint per Host, every cross-cell `404`. The audience question that survives is *sandbox-vs-live on the same host* (hypothesis 1), which is different and still open.
[PARKED] fallback-tier unauthenticated payment-status read: refuted — `device-token` + `x-tpp-userip` with no `Authorization` → `401` on all three status routes; documentation defect only, would be a no-POC rejection.
[PARKED] `api.tech26.de` legacy BOLA (92) and `pay.n26.com` Stripe-forwarded BOLA (85): both still valid and undischarged, retained below the cut only because this cycle's entire new evidence concerns the open-banking tier. Neither is invalidated.
[FINAL] 1. xs2a.tech26.de sandbox/live token audience confusion on a 21-class money-movement API (72 — only hypothesis this cycle backed by a new observation); 2. aisp.tech26.de unbound 180-day refresh chain (70); 3. fallback-tier BOLA with client-asserted `x-tpp-userip` (68). No anonymous result is promoted as a finding; zero secrets obtained this cycle (published `client_id`/PKCE values are public identifiers, not credentials).

## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION

[NEXT] PROBE: `GET https://xs2a.tech26.de/sandbox/oauth2/authorize?client_id=PSDDE-BAFIN-000001&scope=DEDICATED_AISP&code_challenge=w6uP8Tcg6K2QR905Rms8iXTlksL6OD1KOWBxTK7wxPI&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fapp.n26.com%2Flogin&response_type=CODE&state=<random-32-hex>` with `User-Agent` set and no cookies. Expected: `302` to `app.n26.com/login` carrying a `request_id` (sandbox tier only, no customer data, no user authenticated, GET-only). This is the only route on the program that can yield a working token **without** coordinator-provisioned credentials, because the sandbox flow mints its own auth code (`POST /sandbox/psu-interaction/generate-auth-code/{request_id}`). The two follow-on POSTs (generate-auth-code, `/sandbox/oauth2/token`) require sign-off and must not be run against the live `/oauth2/*` tier; stop immediately if any response contains non-sandbox data.

## STEP 6 — LEARNING

[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: the PSD2 **sandbox tier is co-tenant on the production host** at `/sandbox/v1/berlin-group/v1/*` (7 classes `401`, bogus-path control `404`) — retracts my 09-26 "sandbox and production are path-separated".
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: the OAuth2 **authorization plane is anonymously reachable on the production host for both tiers** — `/oauth2/authorize` and `/sandbox/oauth2/authorize` return `401` with documented parameters and `404` without them. Retracts 09-26 "token-minting surface is not anonymously reachable" and proves my own 2-hour-old correction with the precise mechanism: **on this edge the 404 is a missing-parameter response, so the discriminator is parameter presence, not HTTP method.** Generalised rule: a 404 on a param-less GET is evidence of nothing at all.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: 8 previously-unenumerated Berlin-Group classes are live, including `payments/instant-sepa-credit-transfers` and `periodic-payments/sepa-credit-transfers` — the live money-movement surface is 21 classes, not 11, and includes irrevocable instant credit transfer.
[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ {xs2a,aisp,pisp}-staging.tech26.de: all three CNAME to `obnium-mtls-staging-fra-558276106` and connect-timeout 25s / 0 bytes on 443 — source-gated SG, class closed, HUMAN_ONLY.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ n26/psd2-tpp-docs: N26 publishes two registered Berlin-Group `client_id`s (`PSDDE-BAFIN-000001`, `PSDES-BDE-3DFD12`) and a PKCE challenge in its own public repo since 2021-12-16, and the collection's `{{address}}` is the **production** host. Third consecutive instance of the 09-25 rule: the vendor's own corpus is the only enumeration source that produces signal on this program, and `psd2-tpp-docs` also documents a `(Fake) Generate auth code` endpoint, i.e. a credential-free token-mint path in the sandbox tier.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ process: my own [NEXT] probe from last cycle (`POST /oauth2/token`) was mis-designed — a GET on the *authorize* plane of the same host answers the reachability question that the token-endpoint 404 could not, without leaving the read-only envelope. Method-shape questions must be asked of the route that actually carries the documented method, not of a sibling.

## STEP 7 — RISK

[RISK] N26 Bank AG: 92 — the open-banking tier is worse than the KB reflected, and this cycle closed the last "unmapped" gaps. The Berlin-Group production API on `xs2a.tech26.de` is 21 route classes (not 11) including instant and periodic SEPA credit transfers; the **PSD2 sandbox tier is co-resident on the same production host behind the same gateway**; the **authorization plane is anonymously reachable on both tiers**; the **sandbox flow mints its own authorization code with no PSU interaction**, so a token is obtainable with no user and no credential; and the one documented transport control (a qualified client certificate required to establish the connection) is never requested by the server. The blast radius if the audience check between `/sandbox/*` and `/*` is missing is irrevocable payment initiation as an authenticated PSU. Offsetting: still zero validated findings, zero anonymous data access, every read and write path returns `401`, and the two public identifiers carry no secret.
