**STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES**
[HYP] Missing mandatory client-certificate (mTLS) enforcement on the production Berlin-Group XS2A API, with the enforcing component positively identified but the control absent
class: MISCONFIG
asset: xs2a.tech26.de /v1/berlin-group/v1, /sandbox/v1/berlin-group/v1
confidence: 94
reasoning: 3 vhosts share ELB `obnium-mtls-live-fra-328671153` and cert SANs `aisp,xs2a,pisp.tech26.de` (RSA 2048 M04, 2026-02-02→2027-03-03). Anonymous TLS1.3 completes, `No client certificate CA names sent` — no `CertificateRequest` ever issued. N26's own public support page states aisp/pisp "requires implementation of a qualified certificate". New this cycle: the edge is **not** a pass-through — it rejects ambiguous framing (duplicate `Authorization` → `400 text/html server: awselb/2.0`) while app auth failures return `401 len=0 server: istio-envoy`. So the policy-enforcing hop is present and demonstrably enforcing a different rule class, with client-cert authentication not among its rules. All 23+ live and 14+ sandbox route classes answer 401 to an anonymous client.
evidence_needed: proof the 401 bearer gate is the *only* compensating control, i.e. no client-cert binding inside the token; a conformance run showing requests served to a non-QWAC client. Counter-argument to neutralise: the API may deliberately delegate identity to bearer+`client_id` and the ELB name may be vestigial — this cannot be settled anonymously and is the reason confidence is 94, not 99.
verify_steps: `echo | openssl s_client -connect xs2a.tech26.de:443 -servername xs2a.tech26.de 2>&1 | grep -E "(Acceptable client certificate|Verify return code|no client certificate)"` → expect no CertificateRequest; repeat for aisp/pisp. Confirm `server:` header split: duplicate-Authorization GET → expect `awselb/2.0` 400, single GET → `istio-envoy` 401.
impact: Berlin Group XS2A mandates eIDAS-qualified-certificate mTLS on every TPP request; without it any internet client reaches the payment-initiation surface unauthenticated at the transport layer, so a stolen bearer token is replayable from anywhere and TPP identity is unverifiable. Regulatory (PSD2/RTS) plus a direct blast radius over `payments/instant-sepa-credit-transfers` (irrevocable). HIGH; CRITICAL if the bearer is the sole control.
testability: PASSIVE

