**STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE**
- [PARKED] xs2a sandbox/live token-audience confusion: route-identity now **proven** (14 sandbox classes mirror live 1:1) which raises the stakes, but the credential-free mint premise I based it on is **refuted** this cycle — a registered `client_id` is no better than a fabricated one, so there is no anonymous token source and the test is AUTH_HELPED. Folded into the same credentialed session as the mTLS evidence; carrying it separately would duplicate that session. Confidence 74, held not promoted.
- [PARKED] `POST /sandbox/oauth2/token` reachability: still unanswerable by GET; and the authorize-plane 401 shows the gate rejects pre-validation, so a token POST is unlikely to be reachable. Unresolved, not closed.
- [PARKED] `pay.n26.com` Stripe BOLA and `keyless` WS subprotocol replay: unchanged, AUTH_HELPED, below the cut — no new evidence this cycle.
- [FINAL] 1. xs2a.tech26.de missing mTLS enforcement (94, PASSIVE — the only provable-today item). 2. api.tech26.de legacy 15-endpoint BOLA (92, AUTH_HELPED). 3. pisp.tech26.de fallback BOLA with client-asserted anti-fraud (68, AUTH_HELPED).

**STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION**
[NEXT] PROBE: tier-selection and gate-bypass differential via client-supplied forwarding headers on the xs2a edge — `GET https://xs2a.tech26.de/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts` with each of `X-Forwarded-Host: sandbox.tech26.de`, `X-Forwarded-Prefix: /sandbox`, `X-Original-URL: /sandbox/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts`, `X-Rewrite-URL: /sandbox/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts`, `X-Forwarded-Proto: http` (one per request, 1.3 s apart, compare status+`server:`+len against the 401/0/`istio-envoy` control). If the gateway routes on any client-supplied header, the sandbox/live separation becomes defeatable with no token at all and hypothesis "audience confusion" converts from AUTH_HELPED to PASSIVE. Nothing here is mutating; stop on any 2xx/3xx.

**STEP 6 — LEARNING**
- [LEARN] REJECTED OTHER @ xs2a.tech26.de: my own 09-26 premise that the sandbox tier offers a **credential-free** token-mint path is refuted — `PSDDE-BAFIN-000001` with full documented params + PKCE returns `401 len=0` byte-identical to a fabricated client_id, and no parameter variation (bearer, redirect_uri, response_type, live tier) changes it. The authorize plane is gated **before** client/OAuth validation. Retracts "the only route that can yield a working token without coordinator-provisioned credentials."
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: the **sandbox** data plane is **route-identical** to live (14 classes incl. both SEPA credit-transfer initiation classes and periodic payments, 1:1 mirrored), not a reduced mock — so the only thing separating a sandbox token from a live one is a single server-side audience check, with no structural discriminator anywhere in the stack.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: the edge is **two components** — `awselb/2.0` rejects ambiguous framing (duplicate `Authorization` → 400 html) while `istio-envoy` returns every 401. The mTLS gap is therefore not "no edge policy" but "edge policy present, client-cert rule absent".
- [LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ {xs2a,aisp,pisp}.tech26.de `.well-known/{openid-configuration,oauth-authorization-server,jwks.json,psd2-aspsp}`: all `404 len=0` on all three hosts, identical to the bogus-path control — no authorization-server metadata published; class closed.
- [LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ {obnium-mtls-live-fra} cert: SAN list is exactly `aisp,xs2a,pisp.tech26.de`; no unprobed sibling on the cert, and the ELB hostname itself fails TLS verification against it (my client's view only, no server claim).
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ process: generalising the 09-26 "ask the method-shape question of the route that carries the documented method" rule — extend it to *components*: once a differential reveals two `server:` values, subsequent framing questions must be aimed at the hop that demonstrably parses framing. The `awselb/2.0` vs `istio-envoy` split was only visible because I probed the header shape, and it is what turned an absence-of-evidence into a characterisation of the gap.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ process: self-audit rule — when a probe returns `curl` exit 60 / HTTP `000`, record it as **my** TLS failure, not a server finding. The ELB-direct test was discarded on exactly that basis.

**STEP 7 — RISK**
[RISK] N26 Bank AG: 93 — the provable-today risk rose and the speculative risk fell. Provable: the production Berlin-Group XS2A API, its 23 live classes including irrevocable instant SEPA credit transfer, and its route-identical 14-class sandbox twin all answer an anonymous internet client, over an `obnium-mtls-live-fra` ALB that is positively shown to enforce request-hygiene policy but never requests a client certificate, against N26's own published statement that a qualified certificate is required. That is a documented-control gap with a regulatory dimension and is testable with no credential at all. Downgraded: the "sandbox mints its own auth code, so a token needs no user and no credential" claim is refuted — a registered client_id is indistinguishable from a fabricated one and the gate rejects before OAuth validation, so nothing is obtainable anonymously today. Unchanged: the api.tech26.de 15-endpoint BOLA set and the pay.n26.com Stripe boundary remain undischarged and credential-blocked. Still zero validated findings, zero anonymous data access, and every read and write path returns 401.
