## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION
[NEXT] PROBE: test whether the ALB filter is bypassable by URL *form* rather than by notation — `for h in "127.0.0.1" "0x7f.1" "localtest.me"; do for v in "http://$h/" "https://$h/" "//$h/" "/\\$h/" "$h"; do printf '%-28s ' "$v"; curl -s -o /dev/null -m 20 -w '%{http_code} %{size_download}\n' "https://xs2a.tech26.de/oauth2/authorize?client_id=zzz&scope=DEDICATED_AISP&redirect_uri=$v"; sleep 1.2; done; done` plus a control `redirect_uri=https://127.0.0.1/`. A protocol-relative `//127.0.0.1/` returning 401 would show the filter matches only a scheme-prefixed literal and would be a second, simpler bypass class. Read-only, GET only, 16 requests.

## STEP 6 — LEARNING
[LEARN] ACCEPTED OATH @ xs2a.tech26.de: the authorize endpoint performs NO pre-authentication value validation of client_id, scope or redirect_uri. The gate requires BOTH client_id and scope to be present (either missing → 404 len=0) and then demands authentication (401 len=0) regardless of value — `scope=BOGUS`, `zzz`, `DEDICATED_AISPX`, `dedicated_aisp` and space-separated pairs all 401 (twice each), and `?scope=BOGUS` alone 404. This RETRACTS my 09-26 ACCEPTED OATH entry ("validates the scope value while performing no client_id validation"): the 404 is a missing-parameter response, not an unregistered-scope response, and I mis-read a presence discriminator as a value discriminator — the same error class I had already retracted twice on this program (`/oauth2/token`, `generate-auth-code`). Generalised rule: on an endpoint returning 401/404, a 404 must be attributed to a *missing* input dimension and proven with a request varying only presence, before it is ever attributed to an *invalid* value. It was caught this cycle only because a deliberately malformed control (`redirect_uri=http://0x7f.1x/`) happened to return 401 and exposed the contradiction.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de: the redirect_uri loopback/private-host blocklist is enforced at the AWS ALB (`server: awselb/2.0`, 118-byte nginx body, no istio-envoy headers), not by the Berlin-Group AS, and it is incomplete — `0x7f.1` and `0x7f.0.0.1` pass where the whole-string hex `0x7f000001` and the decimal/octal/short forms are blocked, and `localtest.me` passes where the DNS-resolving `127.0.0.1.nip.io` is blocked. The filter's integer parser handles all-hex addresses but not mixed hex+decimal notation. Reproduced 3/3 with interleaved controls.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ process: the 4th consecutive corpus re-read paid off, but the signal came from a file I had never opened (`doc/decoupled/dedicated-aisp.md`), not from the Postman collection and OpenAPI yml that three prior cycles mined exhaustively. The "vendor corpus is the correct enumeration source" rule was already in the KB; the refinement is that the corpus includes *prose* documents carrying control semantics (a documented 403 behaviour, a documented client-controlled state header), and prose is where the logic flaws live — machine-readable route lists were fully exhausted two cycles ago. Rule: when a corpus route map is complete but yields no finding, read the corpus's documentation, not its route lists.

## STEP 7 — RISK
[RISK] N26 Bank AG: 93 — unchanged headline, but the composition changed materially. The provable risk is still the production Berlin-Group XS2A API answering an anonymous internet client over an `obnium-mtls-live-fra` ALB that never issues a TLS CertificateRequest, against N26's own published statement that a QWAC is required. This cycle produced the first non-endpoint-map finding in ~10 days: the OAuth authorization endpoint performs no application-layer validation of client_id, scope or redirect_uri, and the only redirect_uri control in front of it is an edge ALB regex that is bypassable via mixed hex notation and at least one loopback-resolving DNS name — so post-authentication redirect_uri binding is the sole remaining control, unverified, on a surface that includes irrevocable instant SEPA credit transfer. I also had to retract my own 09-26 scope-validation claim as unsound, which is a reminder that the prior cycle's "ACCEPTED OATH" was carried forward at conf 74 without re-derivation. Still zero validated findings, zero anonymous data access, every response 0 bytes. Two coordinator inputs remain outstanding: a TPP/PSU sandbox identity for xs2a, and paired-device grant tokens for api.tech26.de.
