- [NEW] The matcher performs **zero URI parsing**: it over-blocks `https://127.0.0.1@evil.example/` and `https://127.0.0.1.evil.example/` → 403 (effective host is a *public* domain) and under-blocks `https://evil.example@127.0.0.1/` → 401 (effective host **is** loopback). It is a substring/regex match on the raw query value with no userinfo, authority-boundary or host extraction.
