#!/bin/bash
# Read-only GET. Is the 403 value-rule unique to xs2a/oauth2/authorize, or is it a
# host-wide / edge-wide / provider-wide WAF rule? 403 (awselb) vs 401/404 (istio-envoy)
# is the discriminator: the ALB fires pre-routing, so 403 is decisive even on paths
# whose 404 is otherwise uninformative.
