## STEP 1 — DELTA

- **[CHANGED] My 09-27 OATH finding (`redirect_uri` blocklist bypass, conf 88) is REFUTED at the root and RETIRED** — three independent disproofs: (1) **param-name-agnostic** — `?x=https://127.0.0.1/` on the Berlin-Group API path returns the identical `403:118 awselb/2.0` as `?redirect_uri=...`; (2) **path-agnostic** — the 403 fires on `/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts`, not just `/oauth2/authorize`; (3) **host-agnostic** — the same 118-byte body is byte-identical on `app.n26.com`, two unrelated ALBs, `sha256 58bf2215b395dcac74c009aa98701854` (the stock ALB default response). It is a generic AWS ALB WAF value rule, not a redirect_uri control.
- **[NEW] That generic WAF rule is scheme-agnostic but scheme-*requiring***: `foo://127.0.0.1` → **403**, bare `127.0.0.1` → **401**, `//127.0.0.1/` → **401** ⇒ it matches `<scheme>://<private-host>`, i.e. an anti-SSRF pattern rule doing no URI parsing.
- **[NEW] It never blocks remote hosts** — `x=https://evil.example/` → 401 on every host tested ⇒ a remote attacker redirect target was never subject to it anywhere.
- **[NEW] The edge WAF inspects QUERY VALUES ONLY — request headers are not inspected at all.** `TPP-Redirect-URI: https://127.0.0.1/`, `TPP-Redirect-URI: https://169.254.169.254/` and a generic `X-Any: https://127.0.0.1/` control all return `401:0 istio-envoy`, indistinguishable from the no-input baseline, while the *identical value as a query param* returns 403.
- **[NEW] @ n26/psd2-tpp-docs — an entire unread `doc/redirect/` doc set (dedicated-aisp / -cbpii / -pisp).** It establishes the real design: the Dedicated Interface Redirect SCA uses a **cert-only `client_credentials` grant with no authorization code and no `redirect_uri` at all** — *"N26 derives the TPP's `client_id` from the certificate."* `/oauth2/authorize?client_id=&scope=&redirect_uri=` is therefore **not** the documented authorisation plane.
- **[NEW] The real post-SCA redirect target is the TPP-supplied request header `TPP-Redirect-URI`** on `POST /v1/berlin-group/v1/consents` — *"The URI N26 redirects the PSU back to after SCA. Mandatory when `TPP-Redirect-Preferred=true`"* — and its **only documented validation is *"missing or malformed → 400 Bad Request / `FORMAT_ERROR`"***, a syntax check with no documented binding to a registered value. `TPP-State` is echoed back as `?state=`.
