## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

- **RETIRED — `redirect_uri` blocklist bypass (was ACCEPTED OATH conf 88, 09-27):** refuted twice over. The 403 is not a redirect_uri control (param-, path- and host-agnostic; byte-identical body on the unrelated `app.n26.com` ALB), and `/oauth2/authorize` is not the documented authorisation plane for this deployment (cert-only `client_credentials`, no authorization code, no `redirect_uri`). I was characterising a generic provider WAF rule on a plane the vendor says is unused. This is my 4th retraction of this family on this program, which is itself the finding about my method: every one of them came from asserting a mechanism from a salient surface instead of reading what the vendor actually specifies.
- **[PARKED] the 118-byte ALB rule as a finding:** generic provider anti-SSRF WAF behaviour, remote hosts never blocked, and it demonstrably never functioned as a control for this purpose. REJECTED-class (WAF/descriptive behaviour) — retained only as evidence that no edge control covers the real redirect input.
- **[PARKED] `TPP-Redirect-URI`:** real control gap and the strongest new item, but the exploit half needs a bearer token and a POST — outside both the credential supply and the read-only envelope.
- **[PARKED] `X-Sandbox-Transaction-Status` client-controlled payment-status override:** genuine business-logic class on a money flow, every status route 401-gated, header is sandbox-scoped. No anonymous observable.
- **[PARKED] ALB over-blocking** (`https://127.0.0.1@evil.example/` → 403 despite a public effective host): genuine functional defect, but the exploitable direction is client outage (out of scope) and it is now attributable to provider config, not N26 code.
- **[PARKED] `{{space_bg_account_id}}` family, scope-value enumeration oracle, non-conformant scope parser:** all moot after the retirement above; the three scope values are public in `psd2-tpp-docs` anyway.
- **[FINAL] 1)** xs2a.tech26.de — absent mTLS removes the sole TPP-identity control, `client_id` is certificate-derived (conf 94, PASSIVE) — **severity raised this cycle**, no longer "missing second factor" but "missing identity".
- **[FINAL] 2)** xs2a.tech26.de `POST /consents` — `TPP-Redirect-URI` unvalidated beyond syntax, no edge coverage, post-authentication redirect from a trusted origin (conf 78, AUTH_HELPED) — **new, replaces the retired OATH item.**
- **[FINAL] 3)** api.tech26.de 15-endpoint cross-tenant BOLA across three hosts (conf 92, AUTH_HELPED).
- **[FINAL] 4)** pay.n26.com Stripe payment API BOLA (conf 85, AUTH_HELPED).
- Ranking basis for 2 above 3/4 is composition value, not raw confidence: item 2 is only reachable *because* item 1's control is absent, and the pair is the only reportable chain in the program that touches a money-movement surface.

