## STEP 1 — DELTA

**[NEXT] DISCHARGED** — the outstanding probe (is the ALB loopback filter scoped to `redirect_uri`/authorize, or a host-wide rule?) returns a decisive **no**:
- `GET /v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts?x=https://127.0.0.1/` → **403/118 awselb/2.0**; `?x=//127.0.0.1/` and `?x=foo` and `?x=169.254.169.254` → **401/0 istio-envoy**. A *non-OAuth* path, an arbitrary param name `x`, triggers it. **It is not a redirect_uri control.**
- **[NEW]** Estate-wide, not host-wide: `403/118 awselb/2.0` on `api`, `beta-api`, `sapi`, `aisp`, `pisp`, `xs2a` **and** `app.n26.com`, `support.n26.com` (n26.com customer web tier). `fpt.tech26.de` exempt (fixed-response 200 stub, no WAF layer).
- **[NEW]** Filter has **zero scheme semantics**: `a://127.0.0.1/`, `xyz://127.0.0.1/`, `gopher://127.0.0.1/` all → 403. Proves literal substring matching, not URI parsing. `HTTPS://127.0.0.1/` → 403, so it is **case-insensitive** (uppercase is not a bypass — correcting the common assumption).
- **[NEW]** Coverage map: request **path** is inspected (`/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts/https://127.0.0.1/` → 403 awselb; bare `/127.0.0.1/` → 404 istio-envoy = passes). **Request headers are NOT inspected**: `X-Any: https://127.0.0.1/` on `api.tech26.de/api/me` → 401 envoy, byte-identical to no-header control.
- **[CHANGED]** Mechanism of my 09-27/09-26 entries is **reframed**: the anchor is the literal `://`, not integer parsing. Bypass class is precisely *"any loopback/RFC1918/metadata target written without `://` in the request URI"* — scheme-relative `//169.254.169.254/`, path-relative `/127.0.0.1/`, bare `169.254.169.254`, DNS alias `localtest.me`.

