## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

- No hypothesis below 40. No REJECTED class retained. All three carry concrete verify steps.
- **[PARKED]** ALB matcher over-blocking (`https://127.0.0.1@evil.example/` → 403 despite a public effective host): a real functional defect that breaks legitimate clients, but the exploitable direction is outage, which is out of scope, and it harms clients rather than attackers. Kept as the fingerprint of non-parsing inside HYP 2, not reported standalone.
- **[PARKED]** `X-Sandbox-Transaction-Status` client-controlled payment-status override: real business-logic class on a money flow, but every status route is 401-gated and the header is sandbox-scoped. No anonymous observable; needs the same sandbox identity as HYP 2.
- **[PARKED]** "Anti-SSRF filter is weak" as a standalone finding: I have **no proven server-side URL-dereferencing sink anywhere in the estate**. Without one, the filter's incompleteness is a control-quality observation, not a finding. It is retained only as the mechanism half of HYP 2, where a concrete redirect sink does exist. This is a deliberate downgrade, not an oversight.
- **[PARKED]** `{{space_bg_account_id}}` route family: environment file resolves it to the same UUID as `bg_account_id` → identical path shape, already mapped.
- **[FINAL] 1)** xs2a.tech26.de production Berlin-Group XS2A API missing mandatory mTLS enforcement (conf 94, PASSIVE) — the only high-severity item testable with no credential; undischarged.
- **[FINAL] 2)** xs2a.tech26.de authorize plane, live + sandbox: no redirect_uri/client_id/scope validation at the AS; the sole edge filter is an estate-wide `://`-anchored case-insensitive substring matcher with no URI parsing, no scheme semantics and no header coverage, bypassable to `//169.254.169.254/`, RFC1918, IPv4/IPv6 loopback and DNS aliases (conf 86, AUTH_HELPED). **This cycle replaced the 09-26 "integer-parser defect" mechanism, which was wrong, and corrected the 09-27 "bypassed a redirect_uri control" framing — there is no such control to bypass.**
- **[FINAL] 3)** api.tech26.de 15-endpoint cross-tenant BOLA across three hosts sharing one edge tier (conf 92, AUTH_HELPED).
- **[FINAL] 4)** pay.n26.com Stripe payment API BOLA (conf 85, AUTH_HELPED).

