[RISK] N26 Bank AG: **94** — down from 96, and the drop is deliberate and methodological rather than a loss of signal. This cycle produced no new exploitable surface and one fully-validated benign defect, but it removed the evidentiary foundation under nine days of route mapping: the 401 that every route count on this program rested on is a pre-routing path-group gate, so the "21 Bearer-gated route classes", the "8 previously-unenumerated classes", the aisp "4 live classes" and the pisp "5 live classes" are path-group membership restated as route inventory, and one prior negative was a false negative created by the same conflation. Two further of my own controls fell: OPTIONS is not method-agnostic on this mesh, and its 404s were being used to close POST-only routes; and the quarterly-report RAG branch my own last [NEXT] depended on is empty of control statements. I also caught myself one request before filing a false positive — an undocumented `consents-management` prefix that turned out to be the `consents*` group matching a prefix, indistinguishable from a path I had invented to be fake. What survives is stronger for having been tested: the rank-1 mTLS/QWAC finding rests on a TLS handshake observation none of this touches and is now corroborated by a fourth N26-authored control statement in a file no prior cycle had opened; the rank-2 aisp BOLA target was narrowed from an unsound five-class set to the two classes whose path group provably resolves, making it better grounded than the 88 it replaces; and rank 3 gained the program's only end-to-end-validated defect, duplicate contradictory security headers reproduced 6/6. The binding constraint is now unambiguous and I am stating it rather than continuing to probe: **anonymous route enumeration on this mesh is at a hard ceiling**, the vendor prose corpus is exhausted after four consecutive cycles of yield, and every one of the three FINAL items needs a credential at the exploit half. Outstanding coordinator inputs, 