SELF-CRITIQUE NOTE (this is the substantive part): I re-used the 09-26 "OPTIONS is method-agnostic" control on aisp.tech26.de without re-proving it there, exactly the error my own 09-27 learning forbids. The same-batch live control caught it in the same batch. I then tested the control on xs2a and pisp and found it false on ALL THREE. So the KB entry was wrong at its source, not merely over-generalised. Consequence: the "control discovered on one tier must be re-run on every sibling" rule needs strengthening — a control must be re-proved on the host where it will be USED, and a control that has only ever been observed on one host is not a program-level property even if the hosts share an ELB, a cert leaf and a vendor.

[FINAL] 1. xs2a.tech26.de AUTH — mTLS/QWAC client-identity unenforced at transport and application (92). Unchanged headline, evidence upgraded this cycle by N26's own reference client refusing to run without --cert.
[FINAL] 2. pisp.tech26.de AUTH — ROPC + MFA on the fallback PIS host, token-endpoint-only, on the mTLS-free ELB (71). New; blocked on one POST.
[FINAL] 3. api.tech26.de/beta-api/sapi MISCONFIG — published deprecation unfulfilled 2.75 years on the PII/TAN/card family (84). Target asset, proven.
