[RISK] N26 Bank AG: 96 — unchanged, and I want to be precise about why rather than inflate it. Nothing this cycle increased the exposure: every response was either 401 with an error body, 404 empty, or 0 bytes, no data was retrieved, no mutation attempted, and the single most valuable outcome was a retraction of my own route inventory rather than a new attack path. The headline (FINAL#1, xs2a mTLS unenforced against N26's own published control) is unchanged and still provable. What did move is the *quality* of the evidence base, in both directions: the deprecation finding is now proven per host with a same-batch control and rests on a stronger claim than before (the surviving surface is a wildcard namespace of unmeasurable breadth, not a 15-route list), while one of my own recurring conclusions has been formally retracted. That asymmetry — a self-inflicted false negative removed, no new reachability gained — is the honest state of this programme, and the three FINAL items remain AUTH_HELPED at their exploit half. Outstanding coordinator inputs, unchanged and now precisely specified: (1) a test QWAC for xs2a.tech26.de, which is a procurement action and unblocks FINAL#1 outright; (2) paired-device grant tokens for api.tech26.de, needed for FINAL#2 and, given today's topology, the only way the true breadth of the /api/accounts/** namespace can ever be measured; (3) TPP test tokens for the aisp role-separation and BOLA test; and (4) a one-line envelope approval for the single POST in [NEXT], which is the cheapest of the four by an order of magnitude.
