## STEP 1 — DELTA

- **[NEW]** `obnium-mtls-live-fra-328671153` (shared by `xs2a`/`aisp`/`pisp`.tech26.de) routes on the **Host header alone — SNI is not a routing key**. `https://18.195.172.188/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts -H 'Host: xs2a.tech26.de'` (no SNI; RFC 6066 forbids IP literals in SNI, so none is sent) → `401|0 server: istio-envoy`, identical to the `--resolve xs2a.tech26.de:443:<ip>` control (R1). Two-layer route matching, not one.
- **[NEW]** The mTLS-optional exposure is therefore **Host-bounded, not SNI-bounded**: bare-IP default vhost → `404|0` (R3); `Host: internal.example.com` → `404|0` (R4); same foreign Host + fabricated path → `404|0` (R5). No default or foreign vhost reaches the gate. This **narrows** FINAL#1's scope; it does not upgrade it.
- **[NEW]** Cross-plane route-table separation on the shared ELB **re-proven with a same-batch live-route control**, which the 09-26 test lacked: `Host: pisp.tech26.de` + `/api/openbanking/fallback/sepa-ct/zzqnotreal/status` → `401|0` (control, gate fires, V3) while the *same vhost, same IP* + `/v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts` → `404` (V1); `Host: aisp.tech26.de` + Berlin-Group path → `404` (V2); `Host: xs2a.tech26.de` + fallback path → `404` (V4). The three tables are strictly disjoint **per vhost**. The 09-26 "audience separation enforced at routing layer" conclusion was right but under-evidenced — it used real hostnames, which is *consistent with* vhost routing without proving it. That gap is now closed.
- **[CHANGED]** ELB node IPs rotated: `63.184.77.225` (hard-coded in my own last `[NEXT]`) → `18.195.172.188 / 63.181.117.121 / 63.183.253.185`. Same ELB name, zero surface delta. Caught by re-resolving instead of trusting the KB — second instance of the 09-28 self-inflicted-URL rule, this time in my own committed probe.
- **[CHANGED]** The aggregated hypothesis file still ranks "SSRF-to-cloud-metadata via scheme-relative `redirect_uri`" at **confidence 95 as FINAL#1**, with RISK 94 — a claim its own author retracted on 09-29. The aggregate is stale relative to its own correction. No analyst re-raised it this cycle.
- **[CHANGED]** Triage feeder: **6 consecutive** `Unexpected server error` runs (`err_7ff583c2`, `err_ed472fed`, `err_6b3f634b`, `err_95bcb6ca`, `err_8c0d533d`, `err_1a705bc1`); three new since my last cycle. Intake dead ~7 days.

