[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ api.tech26.de/beta-api/sapi: the host's anonymous 401/404 oracle answers exactly one question — **is this URL inside a gate-mounted path pattern** — and never "does this resource exist". Measured this session with a path-shape control rather than the fabricated-noun control I used on 09-28: `/api;/accounts/1/tans` → 404 while `/api/accounts/1/tans` → 401, and `/api/zzqnotreal` → 404 proves the mount is not the `/api` prefix. This sharpens the 09-28 rule rather than repeating it. The operational consequence is a reframing of the enumeration question, and it retires a long-running waste: on a pattern-gated host, probing more resource nouns returns null by construction, because the fabricated-noun control proves the code carries no route information. Nine cycles of noun enumeration on this namespace were structurally incapable of producing a finding. What *is* answerable anonymously is the size of the gated pattern space, and that is the number that determines blast radius. Enumeration should be re-aimed from "which resources exist" to "how much is behind the gate".

[LEARN] REJECTED OTHER @ api.tech26.de: my own 09-27 rule about re-proving controls on siblings nearly produced a fifth repeat of the 09-28 mistake in the opposite direction. I had a `;` differential on api.tech26.de and was one step from writing it up as a family property of the legacy namespace. Re-proving it individually on beta-api and sapi produced identical bytes, which is the correct outcome — but note *why* it is not a finding: both readings (gate-misses-but-router-also-misses, and both-layers-treat-`;`-literally) predict the same `404|0`, and a stripping router would have returned 401. Two hypotheses, one observable, no evidence either way. I am recording the `;` behaviour as a structural fact about gate mounting and explicitly **not** claiming a bypass, because claiming one would be exactly the presence-vs-value error I retracted three times on this programme. A differential is not a bypass until something live is reached through it.

[RISK] N26 Bank AG: 92 — the strongest item (xs2a.tech26.de mTLS collected and discarded) is now closed on all four axes with every measurement reproduced this session, and is reportable as HIGH. The two MEDIUM items are both blocked on credentials the coordinator has not supplied for 28+ consecutive cycles. The material change this cycle is negative and worth stating plainly: I have now proven that the legacy /api/* enumeration axis is structurally exhausted rather than merely unproductive, so no further anonymous probing of that namespace should be scheduled, and the remaining work on it is a credential handoff, not a testing task.
