## STEP 6 — LEARNING

`[LEARN]` ACCEPTED OTHER @ process: my own committed [NEXT] last cycle was already discharged before this cycle began, so the honest opening move was to pick a number already in the knowledge base that had never been re-derived — and I picked my own. The KB had carried "sandbox tier = 7 route classes" for four cycles; re-enumerating against the production class list falsified it, because the original count came from a partial wordlist. This is the 09-25 rule ("a host may only be called route-less for the route table that was actually enumerated") firing on a claim I authored myself, four cycles after I wrote the rule. Generalised: **every count in this knowledge base is a snapshot of some analyst's wordlist, not a property of the target** — including counts I wrote myself and including counts on the *same* host and *the same* endpoint I re-prove every cycle. The number most likely to be wrong is the one that sounds complete.

`[LEARN]` ACCEPTED OTHER @ xs2a.tech26.de: a control discovered on the production tier must be re-run on the sandbox tier *before it is described as host-level*, and this cycle the re-run inverted the finding rather than confirming it. I had 5 cycles of route-aware 401/404 evidence on the live plane and treated it as a property of the host. Re-running it on `/sandbox/` was necessary — and separately, re-enumerating the sandbox tier against the production class list (rather than a sandbox-specific wordlist) is what surfaced the real delta. The 09-27 rule I wrote ("re-run the control on each co-tenant tier") was correct but I had applied it only to the ALB blocklist finding, not to the route-awareness finding, because the latter felt too well-established to be host-specific. Generalised: **a control re-run can confirm, invert, or extend; the expected outcome must not influence whether it is run, and "too well-established to be host-specific" is the exact prior that makes this failure invisible.**

## STEP 7 — RISK

`[RISK]` N26 Bank AG: 92 — unchanged from last cycle in aggregate, but the composition shifted: the previously-reported HIGH (xs2a.tech26.de mTLS collected and discarded, PASSIVE-VERIFIED, four axes closed) remains the top item, and it is now materially worse-scoped by this cycle's finding that the sandbox tier co-tenant carries the **full** payment-initiation surface on the same optional-mTLS edge rather than a reduced 7-class subset. Two MEDIUM AUTH_HELPED items (sandbox/live tier separation, PKCE ignored by the pre-auth gate) are new or newly-scoped. All anonymous axes on all in-scope assets are now exhausted — the ungated regions of the legacy namespace are provably empty, the sandbox class list is bounded, and the pre-auth gate is fully characterised at two parameters. The pipeline remains blocked on credential/scope supply, not on further probing; the triage feeder has now failed 19+ consecutive runs (`err_680948db` latest), so hypothesis intake is dead independently of the credential gap.
