## STEP 6 — LEARNING

[LEARN] ACCEPTED OATH @ xs2a.tech26.de: the ALB substring blocklist is **query-string-scoped**, not request-scoped, and the field it inspects is not the field the production redirect flow uses. Proven in one batch with paired invented-field controls in both directions: query `foo=https://127.0.0.1@evil.example/` → `403|118` awselb/2.0 (field-agnostic, confirmed 09-29), while header `X-Foo: https://127.0.0.1@evil.example/` → `401|0` istio-envoy and header `TPP-Redirect-URI: http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/` → `401|0` (headers not inspected). This **supersedes** the 09-29 retraction: that entry was right that no OAuth control was bypassed *in the query parameter*, and wrong to conclude no redirect control exists — `doc/sandbox.md` and `doc/redirect/dedicated-aisp.md` (both never opened before this cycle) document a production redirect destination carried in the `TPP-Redirect-URI` **header**, with `TPP-State` echoed to it and `error=access_denied` on failure. Generalised rule, and the fourth instance of this programme's recurring error family: **before characterising a filter's parsing, prove its channel.** I spent 09-26 → 09-29 (four cycles, ~25 requests) refining notation on a query string, and the decisive dimension — header vs query string — cost three requests and had been sitting in unread vendor prose the whole time.

[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ n26/psd2-tpp-docs: `doc/decoupled/dedicated-cbpii.md` and `doc/sandbox.md` (both never opened by any cycle) reveal a third dedicated role, CBPII Confirmation of Funds, with its own consent subtree `/v1/berlin-group/v1/consents/confirmation-of-funds{,/{id},{id}/status,{id}/authorisations,/authorisations/{id}}`, live on production at `401|0` with an 8-11ms app-layer timing signature against a 1ms same-batch bogus-path 404, and mirrored on the sandbox tier. The KB's "21 classes complete" map came from the Postman/OpenAPI branches and silently excluded this subtree — a *third* confirmation that a route map derived from one corpus branch is a snapshot, not a bound, and that `grep -c "confirmation-of-funds" ctx.txt` returning 0 was the cheapest possible check that the map was incomplete.

[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ xs2a.tech26.de `/v1/berlin-group/v1/funds-confirmations`: `404|0` on both tiers. Retained as explicitly **not** evidence of absence — the corpus documents it as `POST`, and this programme's own twice-retracted rule (see `api/mfa/challenge`) is that a 404 on a GET proves nothing for a documented-POST route. Recorded so a later cycle does not mistake this for a closed route.

