[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ `app.n26.com`: **two KB claims about this surface were wrong in shape, and I am retracting both.** (1) KB: "`/wl/open-banking/*` (`/{aisp,cbpii,pisp}` each 302 → login)". False on both counts — `pisp` is not a one-segment leaf (it is three two-segment leaves under `pisp/`), and the AISP/CBPII leaves do **not** redirect to login at hop 1; they redirect to the same path minus `/wl` with no login hop. The earlier "302 → login" was an artifact of following a redirect through the class-C `/feed` fallback into `/login`, i.e. the finding described the *fallback*, not the leaf. (2) KB: "redirect is rebuilt server-side from the matched route path". True but incomplete: on class B the builder carries the **entire request query** into `redirect`, re-encoded — nested `&` becomes `%2526` (`state=a%26redirect%3D…` → `state=a%2526redirect%253D…%26authType%3DXS2A`). Both errors are the 09-25 generic-wordlist error and the cross-day-comparison error recurring on a host nobody had characterised before.
