[LEARN] ACCEPTED AUTH @ `xs2a.tech26.de` + `api.tech26.de`: the edge gate is **route-level and GET-only**, now proven rather than inferred — the KB called it a "GET-scoped wildcard middleware" but every prior probe was itself a GET. Same-path, same-batch, three-method legs: `GET /v1/berlin-group/v1/accounts` → `401|0` (xs2a) and `GET /api/accounts/1/tans` → `401|211` (api), while `HEAD` and `OPTIONS` on those **same gated paths** → `404|0` empty (`istio-envoy` / `envoy`), identical to the fabricated-path legs. Because a `HEAD`/`OPTIONS` miss returns `404` and not `401`, this is method matching on the route, not a middleware that skips preflight — the distinction matters, because it means **no documented POST on either host is covered by the edge gate at all.** Every write on these hosts, including `POST /oauth2/token` and all Berlin-Group consent/payment POSTs, has the application layer as its only access control. This raises the priority of the cert-only token-mint hypothesis and bounds what a `401` on a GET can ever prove about the write plane.
