## STEP 1 — DELTA

```
[NEW] app.n26.com `/login` — GraphQL-Relay form POSTs to `/graphql` (`__mutation=requestBiometricChallengeMutation`) with hidden `__successRedirect` / `__failureRedirect`. The `redirect` query param is copied into BOTH, unvalidated: `?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fevil.example%2Fprobe` → `value="/login?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fevil.example%2Fprobe&amp;verifyLogin=1"`, size invariant 316306B (3/3). Protocol-relative `//evil.example/probe` likewise accepted (316290B). 12 anonymous GETs, UA set, `Accept-Encoding: identity`, 6s pacing.
[NEW] app.n26.com edge query-string content filter characterised: `?redirect=%22%3E%3Cimg...` and `?redirect=javascript%3A...` → `403|520` nginx page, byte-identical md5 `2e40045e…`; absolute/protocol-relative URLs pass. Host-specific measurement — NOT transferred from the tech26.de `403|118 awselb` rule.
[NEW] app.n26.com `/login` reflection is a raw-query-slice echo, not a parsed value: `?redirect=%22` and `?redirect="` both surface as `%22`, `&quot;` count 0, hidden-input attribute never terminates early → no attribute breakout, no DOM-XSS via this parameter.
[CHANGED] RETRACTION: KB line "attacker-supplied `redirect=` is discarded" was measured on `/open-banking*` only and does NOT hold on `/login`. Same control, different path — the 09-28 "a control is a property of the request path it was measured on" rule violated by my own prior entry.
[CHANGED] `/login` baseline determinism control: 3 independent fetches all `200|316210B` (md5 varies — embedded per-request `_csrf`/challenge token). Size channel is trustworthy on this page, unlike the 09-30 gzip-variance near-miss.
[CHANGED] Field-scoping control: `?zzz=https%3A%2F%2Fevil.example%2Fprobe` → `200|316210B` (baseline-identical), 0 reflections. The echo is scoped to the `redirect` field, not a generic query-string reflect.
NO_DELTA — xs2a/aisp/pisp/api/beta-api/sapi/pay/flags/engagementplatform not probed this cycle; no inbound signal, state unchanged per inventory.
