## STEP 6 — LEARNING

```
[LEARN] ACCEPTED OATH @ `app.n26.com/login`: the `redirect` query parameter is copied unvalidated into the GraphQL-Relay `__successRedirect` AND `__failureRedirect` hidden inputs (absolute and protocol-relative external hosts both accepted), on a form that POSTs to `/graphql` with `requestBiometricChallengeMutation`. Field-scoped by control (`?zzz=` → baseline-identical, 0 reflections) and size-deterministic (baseline 316210B ×3; redirect legs invariant). `__failureRedirect` means the off-site bounce survives a failed login. Confidence bounded at 75 because the relay's execution is spec-inferred, not observed.
[LEARN] REJECTED OTHER @ `app.n26.com/login` (DOM-XSS via `redirect`): closed with evidence rather than assumed. The page echoes the raw query slice unparsed — `?redirect=%22` and a literal `"` both surface as `%22`, `&quot;`=0, the hidden-input attribute never terminates — and the edge drops `<`/`javascript:` with a byte-identical `403|520` nginx page. No breakout, no script execution path.
[LEARN] REJECTED OTHER @ my own KB: the line "attacker-supplied `redirect=` is discarded" was measured on `/open-banking*` and does not hold on `/login`. Sixth instance of the 09-28 rule — a control is a property of the request path it was measured on, not of the parameter name. The generalisation was wrong in the direction that *hides* a finding, which is the expensive direction: read literally, the old line told a later cycle the parameter was safe everywhere on the host.
[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ `app.n26.com` edge: a query-string content filter that returns `403|520` (nginx body) on markup and `javascript:` in the query while passing absolute and protocol-relative URLs. Recorded as host-specific on its own measurements; explicitly NOT transferred from the tech26.de `403|118 awselb` rule despite the shared 403/ALB family, per the same rule.
